# Reports center (R01..R15 + value-added)
ReportInternalTransfers=Internal transfers
ReportTreasuryByWarehouse=Treasury by warehouse/store
ReportActivityByWarehouse=Financial activity by warehouse
ReportCategoryNvsN1=Category comparison N vs N-1
ReportReconciliation=Bank reconciliation
ReportCashClosing=Daily cash closing
ReportUserActivity=User entry activity
ReportReviewMode=Management review mode
ReportDescriptionTitle=This report allows you to
ReportWhatFor=What is this report for?
ReportTipR01=Detailed journal of all entries for an account or cash register over the selected period, with running balance after each operation, in/out totals and reconciliation rate. Serves as the official accounting record of movements.
ReportTipR02=Real-time snapshot of your treasury: balance of each account and cash register, consolidated equivalent in the main currency, 7-day trend, last movement and accounts below their minimum alert threshold.
ReportTipR03=Trend of inflows, outflows and net flow per account, grouped by week, month, quarter, year or over the whole period. Helps spot cash-tension periods.
ReportTipR04=List of all internal transfers between accounts and cash registers: amounts in both currencies, exchange rate actually applied and gap with the system rate, to catch entry errors.
ReportTipR05=Estimate of realized FX gains and losses on foreign-currency operations, comparing the rate on the operation date with the current rate.
ReportTipR06=History of all exchange-rate changes: old and new rate, variation in %, who changed it and the source (manual or API).
ReportTipR07=Treasury aggregated by warehouse/store, summing all linked accounts and cash registers, with the consolidated equivalent in the main currency. Ideal to steer a network of outlets.
ReportTipR08=Comparison of financial activity (inflows, outflows, net flow, number of operations) of each warehouse/store over the period, to spot the most active or atypical outlets.
ReportTipR09=Breakdown of inflows and outflows by accounting category (tags), to identify your main revenue sources and expense items.
ReportTipR10=Comparison of category flows between the current period (N) and the equivalent previous period (N-1), with the gap in value and percentage.
ReportTipR11=Regulatory audit trail: full history of creations, modifications and deletions on accounts and entries, with user, date, affected field and before/after values.
ReportTipR12=Automatically detected anomalies (duplicates, unusual amounts, abnormal rates, negative balances…), with severity level and processing status.
ReportTipR13=Bank reconciliation level per account: number of reconciled and unreconciled entries and reconciliation rate, to track matching against statements.
ReportTipR14=Official daily cash-closing statement: movements, opening and closing balance, totals, to print and have signed by the cashier and manager.
ReportTipR15=Data-entry activity per user: number of operations, first and last activity, to measure workload and spot unusual behavior.
ReportTipReview=Consolidated document ready for the management meeting, combining in a single output the dashboard (R02), period flows (R03), treasury by warehouse (R07) and the N/N-1 comparison (R10).
ReportDailyCashMatrix=Daily cash position by account
ReportTipR16=Daily cash matrix: for each day of the period, the inflows and outflows of every account/cash register, the total flow converted to the main currency, then the consolidated end-of-day balance per currency and its equivalent in the main currency. A TOTAL row sums the period flows and shows the closing balances.
